  "title": "R14c: orchestrator/jev_points.py \u2014 experimental Jev decision points (scout necessity, context escalation, review escalation, planner relaunch), shadow by default, escalate-only in active, fail-open (Phase I P7)",
  "spec": "Why: Phase I P7 names four experimental Jev decision points introduced independently: scout necessity, context escalation, review escalation (never overriding the mandatory security review) and Planner relaunch. Today planner_runs.jev_triage (orchestrator/planner_runs.py:432-460) records one generic shadow choice for scouts_done/held/closable decision kinds and decision.py has no Jev use; nothing covers the four named points (audit T-0573).\nWhat: new pure module orchestrator/jev_points.py using jev.ask (fail-open, returns None on any failure) and decision_log.record(kind=\"routing\" is wrong here: use kind \"scout\" for scout necessity, \"review_plan\" for review escalation, \"strategy\" for context escalation and planner relaunch, with extra={\"point\": name}).\n- POINTS = (\"scout_necessity\", \"context_escalation\", \"review_escalation\", \"planner_relaunch\"); each has its own mode under [jev.points] <point> = off|shadow|active (default shadow; unknown -> shadow) and a typed question set (noul probabilities) with a bounded, redacted state: task title, spec[:600] via jev.redact, acceptance count, scope list, complexity, task_class, memory titles, deterministic evidence supplied by the caller (e.g. scout_evidence.reuse_check result, packet size, review plan). Never file contents.\n- ask(point, task, evidence, *, cfg=None, ask_fn=jev.ask) -> {\"point\", \"mode\", \"signals\", \"confidence\", \"suggestion\", \"applied\": bool, \"error\"}: suggestion per point: scout_necessity -> \"launch\"|\"skip\"; context_escalation -> \"expand\"|\"keep\"; review_escalation -> \"add_review\"|\"keep\"; planner_relaunch -> \"relaunch\"|\"wait\". off -> no call, suggestion None. shadow -> call and record, applied False. active -> applied True only for escalating suggestions (launch a scout that deterministic reuse says is unnecessary is NOT escalation and stays a suggestion; expand context, add a review, relaunch are escalations); de-escalations (skip scout, keep smaller context, fewer reviews) are never applied; review_escalation can never reduce reviews or replace the security review (documented and tested); any failure -> suggestion None, error set, applied False.\n- Every call records a decision_log row with candidates (the two options), hard_constraints ([\"security_review_deterministic\", \"required_reviews_floor\"] for review_escalation), deterministic evidence, jev signals, selected, reason, confidence, mode.\n- summary(root=STATE) -> per point {n, agreement with deterministic evidence where comparable, mean_confidence} from decision rows, for later evaluation.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_jev_points.py::test_default_shadow_records_suggestion_without_applying \u2014 empty config: scout_necessity calls ask once, returns suggestion skip with applied False and writes a decision row with extra.point",
    "tests/test_jev_points.py::test_off_mode_makes_no_call \u2014 mode off for a point: ask_fn not called, suggestion None",
    "tests/test_jev_points.py::test_active_applies_only_escalations \u2014 active review_escalation with add_review applies True; active scout_necessity with skip applies False; active context_escalation with keep applies False",
    "tests/test_jev_points.py::test_review_escalation_never_reduces_or_replaces_security_review \u2014 a suggestion of fewer reviews is coerced to keep, hard_constraints list security_review_deterministic, and the deterministic review count in the returned evidence is unchanged",
    "tests/test_jev_points.py::test_fail_open_and_privacy \u2014 ask_fn returning None yields error set, suggestion None, applied False; the state passed to ask_fn is redacted and contains no file contents"
  ],
